\details{
\subsection{The revision trap, in one paragraph}{

FRED serves the \emph{latest revised} value of every observation. Most macro series
(money supply, unemployment, jobless claims, financial-conditions indices) are
revised — sometimes heavily, sometimes across their whole history — long after
first release. So "what does the API say GDP growth was in 2008-Q1 today" is
\strong{not} "what a trader knew in 2008-Q1": today's history embeds numbers nobody
had then. Backtesting on it is look-ahead by construction. ALFRED (ArchivaL
FRED) fixes this: it serves every value \emph{as it was known at each point in
time}. This package exposes that as-known-then surface directly through
\link{FredSeries}'s \code{get_series_vintages()}.
}

\subsection{What is covered}{
\itemize{
\item \link{FredSeries}: the client. \code{get_series()} (observations at any real-time
window — the latest values are simply today's window), the headline
\code{get_series_vintages()} (the ALFRED as-known-then long form, offset-paged so
a whole-history matrix that exceeds FRED's per-response row cap streams back
safely), \code{get_series_info()} (metadata: frequency, units, revision cadence),
\code{search_series()}, \code{get_releases()}, and \code{get_release_dates()}.
}
}

\subsection{Sync and async}{

Every request-making method supports both a synchronous mode (returns a
\code{data.table}) and an asynchronous mode (returns a \link[promises:promise]{promises::promise} resolving
to the same \code{data.table}), selected by the \code{async} argument at construction.
See \link{FredSeries} for the mechanism.
}

\subsection{The API key}{

Every FRED endpoint requires a free API key (a 32-character lowercase
credential from \url{https://fred.stlouisfed.org/docs/api/api_key.html}). Supply it
as the \code{FRED_API_KEY} environment variable or the \code{api_key} constructor
argument. FRED throttles at 120 requests/minute per key. A missing or invalid
key surfaces as a typed \link{fred_conditions} error (an HTTP 400 whose body names
the key problem).
}
